PHYSICS_AND_ARCHITECTURE_CHANGE_SUMMARY:
example/testexample.jl explicitly enables czm.geo_nonlinear=true and czm.j2_plasticity=true.
PlasticState carries committed Cauchy stress together with eps_p/kappa.
The same Gauss-point material integration supplies local second-Piola S, consistent tangent, and trial state.
S remains assembly-local; output only projects committed Cauchy state and does not rerun plasticity.
basic/load-substep/geo arc-length use committed/trial buffers and commit atomically only on convergence.
The obsolete post-solve commit_plastic bulk assembly is removed.
Later Cycle phases initialize history from an existing committed state instead of adding a new NaN prefix.
The yield cutoff is relative to trial/yield stress scale and is invariant under equivalent stress-unit rescaling.

